/*
 * Dynamic color is the default path (see InstaDMTheme): on Android 12+ the
 * scheme is generated by the system from the user's wallpaper, so every
 * Material You app on the device shares the same palette.
 *
 * The two schemes below are only the fallback for API 24-30. They are outputs
 * of the Material tonal algorithm for a single seed, Google Blue #0B57D0, not
 * hand-picked values: every role is a tonal stop of the same tonal palette, so
 * the roles stay consistent with each other and with the components that
 * derive colors from them (containers, elevation, disabled states).
 *
 * The vibrant variant is used because the default tonal-spot variant clamps
 * the seed's chroma and turns that blue into a desaturated navy (#495D92);
 * vibrant keeps the saturation Google apps render (#0056D2 light, #B2C5FF
 * dark).
 *
 * surfaceTint is pinned to surface so tonal elevation stays a neutral container
 * step instead of washing every elevated surface with a blue overlay.
 */

